## Excuse

If anyone violates these terms, the licensor may excuse
them, but only if the licensor agrees to excuse them in
writing. Excusing violators doesn't affect the licensor's
rights against anyone else who violates these terms.

## Patent License

The licensor grants you a patent license for the software
that covers patent claims the licensor can license, or
becomes able to license, that you would infringe by using
the software.

## Noncommercial Purposes

Any purpose is a noncommercial purpose other than the
commerce-related purposes defined below. The licensor may
authorize commercial purposes by licensing the software
under other terms.

A commercial purpose is one that is primarily intended for
commercial advantage or compensation. Commercial advantage
includes any revenue-generating use, such as selling copies
of the software, or providing the software as part of a paid
service or paid product. Compensation includes any form of
consideration, such as payment, equity, or other benefits in
exchange for use of the software.

## Fair Use

You may have "fair use" rights for the software under the
law. These terms do not limit them.

## No Other Rights

These terms do not allow you to sublicense or transfer any
of your licenses to anyone else, or prevent the licensor
from granting licenses to anyone else.  These terms do not
imply any other licenses.

## Patent Defense

If you make any written claim that the software infringes or
contributes to infringement of any patent, your patent
license for the software granted under these terms ends
immediately. If your company makes such a claim, your patent
license ends immediately for work on behalf of your company.

## Violations

The first violation of these terms results in a warning,
unless the licensor decides otherwise. The second violation
of these terms results in immediate termination of all your
licenses under these terms, unless the licensor decides
otherwise.

## No Liability

***As far as the law allows, the software comes as is, without
any warranty or condition, and the licensor will not be liable
to you for any damages arising out of these terms or the use
or nature of the software, under any kind of legal claim.***

## Definitions

The **licensor** is the individual or entity offering these
terms, and the **software** is the software the licensor makes
available under these terms.

**You** refers to the individual or entity agreeing to these
terms.

**Your company** is any legal entity, sole proprietorship, or
other kind of organization that you work for, plus any
organizations that have control over, are under the control
of, or are under common control with that organization.
**Control** means ownership of substantially all the assets
of an entity, or the power to direct its management and
policies by vote or otherwise. If control is such an entity
exists only for the benefit of a users' community or similar
purpose, it is not considered control for these purposes,
specifically excluding community-owned and membership
organizations, cooperatives, and nonprofit organizations.
